  "change_summary": [
    "Enforce exactly two videos and two podcasts from distinct canonical shows, with direct selected-item URLs and matching exact item/source identities.",
    "Use one strict research_cutoff_at recorded during unfinished EDITORIAL; reject changes or removal on resume and bind it across state, current bundle, records and retained evidence.",
    "Apply the independent 72-hour video limit and exact 600/900/1200-second bands; require fallback rationales and reject older or longer candidates without borrowing article policy.",
    "Apply podcast 48-hour preferred, seven-day fallback and exceptional 30-day freshness with required rationales and no listening-duration ceiling; preserve the existing observed-runtime requirement.",
    "Retain original metadata and precision; model date-only publication as a conservative interval with timezone/DST handling and reject unresolved outer-boundary eligibility.",
    "Read and hash bounded evidence files; require substantive support and current content-pass review bound to exact media copy, selected story meaning and complete referenced evidence contents.",
    "Keep Summary, Why it matters and Connection to the Brief separate; reject normalized duplicate pairs and require the existing content pass to assess semantic distinction.",
    "Project all three fields, original source dates, exact Duration, direct safe links and separate written-podcast read time through existing reader pages, feeds and archive data without changing the vendored renderer.",
    "Use the same pure media validation from CONTENT selection and compiler bundle admission, with a read-only CLI and explicit current/historical receipt status.",
    "Admit only exact registered historical v1 bundles under their recorded contracts; reject unregistered version downgrades and preserve terminal state and asset bytes."
  ],
